{
  "_doc": "Placeable ship components. Content is data: add an entry here and it can be placed. size is [w, h] in cells at rotation 0 (a crew body is 2x2 cells, so a 1-cell corridor is too narrow). power: positive produces, negative consumes. priority: lower is powered first when power is short (0 for producers and zero-power parts). tier: 1 to 3 (Mk1 to Mk3). family groups related parts. manned: works better with crew. stats: numbers read by the systems that use the part. line: scrap, standard or neon (data/lines.json). hp: system health, at 0 it is disabled until repaired. heat_limit: overheats at this heat. heat_per_s: heat gained per second while running. cooling: heat lost per second. stats.cooling_bonus: extra cooling every part in the same room gets (radiator). Shield stats: stats.layers (bubble layers), stats.sectors (1, 2, 4 or 8: how many sectors the bubble is split into, bow first and clockwise: Mk1 and scrap 1, Mk2 2, Mk3 and Neon 4, and 8 for the Mk5 and the late uniques; the best powered generator sets it, and each sector holds layers x its balance weight, docs/CONTENT.md section 4) and stats.recharge (seconds until a used layer is back, default 2.0; lower is faster). unique: true marks a found-or-traded item that has no recipe. effects: tags the combat code reads for a unique or special part (for weapons they live in weapons.json). A weapon part needs an entry in weapons.json under the same id. abilities: optional list of {id, name, type (active or passive), key (engine, shield or utility: the combat key that triggers an active one), duration and cooldown in seconds (the cooldown starts when the effect ends), effects, side_effects, operator_needs, event} (see docs/CONTENT.md section 5 and scripts/sim/abilities.gd). effects: stat_mult {thrust or power: factor} on this part, shield_layer (extra layers), charge_mult (weapon cooldown factor), evasion_add. side_effects: a list of {type, rate} applied per second while it runs: drain_o2 (fraction of the room's air lost per second), heat, power_spike (extra draw), fire_risk (chance per second), self_damage (hp per second). operator_needs: traits a crew member manning the part must have; a|b means either. blurb: one line of flavour. Ram parts (docs/CONTENT.md 4e) read stats.ram_deal (damage dealt to the other ship in a collision, as a multiple), stats.tether_s (seconds it latches on after a hit), stats.ram_take (multiple of ram damage taken by the ship's plain cells while the part is powered) and stats.no_knock (1: crew take no knock from a ram while it is powered). mount (weapons and engines): {outside: [w, h], outside_hp} makes the part two linked halves through a hull wall of any thickness (docs/CONTENT.md 4f). size is the INSIDE half (on the floor, crewed and wired); the outside half sits in space at the outer wall face, outward is UP at rotation 0, takes the visible hits with its own outside_hp and is only ever disabled; a direct hit on a disabled inside half wrecks the part. Engine stats: thrust, and fuel_mult (a jump of the Drift costs 1 x the thrust-weighted mean fuel_mult of the powered engines; an engine without one counts as 1.0; docs/waves/engines_1.md). quirk: a line of text saying why a part is off its balance band (data/balance.json), which exempts it.",
